  "seminaryName": "St. John's Seminary",
  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "Winter is a wall of grey from Advent to Lent, and the pastor shovels the church steps himself because the plow guy does the school first.",
      "The one week of spring arrives in May, and the whole diocese schedules its First Communions in it.",
      "Summer is the Cape and the collections fall by a third, and the pastor covering three parishes learns which roads flood.",
      "October is the reason people stay: the leaves on the Common, the light on the harbor, and the Sox in or out of it."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "The eight o'clock in the old parishes is forty people who have sat in the same pews since Cushing; the noon Mass in Portuguese fills the same church to the doors.",
      "In Wellesley the ushers are lawyers and the collection is by envelope and app; in Lynn it is cash and a second collection for someone's surgery.",
      "The Vietnamese Mass in Dorchester runs long and ends with a meal in the hall that the pastor is expected to open."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The priests of Boston talk about the men who left, the men who were taken away, and the men who stayed, in that order, and never in front of the young.",
      "Half of them went to Brighton and half to Weston, and the difference still shows at dinner.",
      "They know every closed church by name and can tell you what it is now: condos, a mosque, a climbing gym."
    ]
  },
